//!   matches by name. `cli_opt_parser_next` parses `--opt` against a list of specs all named
//!   `opt`, each with no value to write, and returns the first spec the macro accepts, or
//!   none; the port answers with the first spec whose kind `is_option`. Each list is a subset
//!   of the seven kinds a listed spec can have, in order and reversed.
